{"kind":"school-course","course":"Uuidna","wing":"Uuidna.lean","title":"Uuidna","principle":"The vortex algebra","skills":["clay-reflection","coins","foundational","involution","neuro","quantum","reflection","science-pairs","vortex","z9-ring"],"level":100,"band":"100–999 steps","rank":117,"lessons":[{"key":"seats_pigeonhole","name":"the pigeonhole seat bound 2^b: 2^8=256, 2^0=1, 2^10=1024","why":null,"statement":"(2:Nat)^8 = 256 ∧ (2:Nat)^0 = 1 ∧ (2:Nat)^10 = 1024","address":"8b402e01-fada-8aa8-a318-da4ab72162fa","skill":"foundational","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":47,"length":4}},{"key":"diamond_involution","name":"the diamond r(d)=10−d is an involution on 1..9 with unique fixed point 5","why":null,"statement":"(List.range' 1 9).all (fun d => 10 - (10 - d) == d) ∧ ((List.range' 1 9).filter (fun d => 10 - d == d)) = [5]","address":"ce9a68df-3423-828b-a61d-7a86be3cb05b","skill":"involution","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":107,"length":1}},{"key":"hodge_bound","name":"Hodge edge: a class can meet the type condition yet lie outside the algebraic span [1,0,1]","why":null,"statement":"((0:Int)+1 = 1) ∧ (∀ c : Int, c ∈ [(-3:Int),-2,-1,0,1,2,3] → ¬ (c*1 = 0 ∧ c*0 = 1 ∧ c*1 = 1))","address":"fe4cc588-8d56-8b58-8c94-92640d7fb05c","skill":"clay-reflection","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":null},{"key":"billing_arith","name":"billing arithmetic: bits saved 1024−1=1023, 10⁶−1=999999; the two coins = 1+1","why":null,"statement":"(1024 - 1 = 1023) ∧ (1000000 - 1 = 999999) ∧ (2 = 1 + 1)","address":"e28b81a1-80f4-89d8-bc65-9324b277998a","skill":"coins","tex":"1024 - 1 = 1023 \\quad\\land\\quad 1000000 - 1 = 999999 \\quad\\land\\quad 2 = 1 + 1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1024</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1023</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1000000</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>999999</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":54,"length":1}},{"key":"div_by_zero_is_the_reflection","name":"division by zero in ℤ/9 is the diamond reflection x/0 = 10−x — a finite residue with fixed points {0,5}","why":null,"statement":"divZero 0 = 0 ∧ divZero 9 = 1 ∧ divZero 8 = 2 ∧ divZero 5 = 5 ∧ divZero 1 = 9 ∧ (List.range' 1 9).all (fun x => divZero x == 10 - x) ∧ ((List.range 10).filter (fun x => divZero x == x)) = [0, 5]","address":"59bcb4b2-06c8-8eda-8987-fdfd34d0d2fe","skill":"reflection","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":192,"length":1}},{"key":"units_z9","name":"the units of ℤ/9 (the residues with an inverse) are exactly {1,2,4,5,7,8} — computed by search","why":null,"statement":"(List.range 9).filter (fun d => (List.range 9).any (fun e => (d * e) % 9 == 1)) = [1,2,4,5,7,8]","address":"f66062ba-8cf0-895b-b7d5-98208bcb8b04","skill":"vortex","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":93,"length":1}},{"key":"involution_group","name":"the critical-strip reflections σ, τ, κ form a Klein four-group; τ fixes the line a=1","why":null,"statement":"sig (sig (3,7)) = (3,7) ∧ tau (tau (3,7)) = (3,7) ∧ kap (kap (3,7)) = (3,7) ∧ sig (kap (3,7)) = tau (3,7) ∧ tau (kap (3,7)) = sig (3,7) ∧ (sig (1,5)).1 = 1 ∧ tau (1,9) = (1,9) ∧ tau (0,4) = (2,4) ∧ (0:Int) ≠ 1 ∧ (2:Int) ≠ 1","address":"dc823fae-9c43-88e6-9a57-c1bff1a022ab","skill":"involution","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":null},{"key":"involute_centre","name":"an index reflection i ↔ (n−1−i) has exactly one centre iff n is odd (fixed-count = n mod 2)","why":null,"statement":"(List.range 12).all (fun n => ((List.range n).filter (fun i => 2*i + 1 == n)).length = n % 2)","address":"f84dbe7d-edc7-838a-9cad-a881db0411f9","skill":"involution","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":91,"length":1}},{"key":"division_by_zero","name":"division by zero EXISTS: total integer 1000/0=0, and 0 (and the zero-divisor 3) have no inverse in ℤ/9","why":null,"statement":"(1000 / 0 = 0) ∧ (0 / 0 = 0) ∧ (List.range 9).all (fun x => (0 * x) % 9 != 1) ∧ (List.range 9).all (fun x => (3 * x) % 9 != 1)","address":"563c6a6e-26c0-88a9-b358-f95ba1a9e361","skill":"reflection","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":119,"length":1}},{"key":"light_faster_than_uuidna","name":"light c=299792458 m/s beats uuidna even at t=0 — k/0=0 (a finite floor), never ∞, so no fake FTL","why":null,"statement":"(299792458 : Nat) > 0 ∧ (List.range 64).all (fun t => 1000 / t < 299792458) ∧ (1000 / 0 = 0)","address":"e484f5f5-c845-885e-922a-7040dbec1d51","skill":"science-pairs","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":90,"length":1}},{"key":"ns_spike","name":"Navier–Stokes edge: bounded energy 1/n falls while the peak n rises — integer inequalities, not a solution","why":null,"statement":"(1*2 < 1*4) ∧ (4 > 2) ∧ (1*4 = 4) ∧ (1*3 < 1*9) ∧ (9 > 3)","address":"0bfe6422-0e95-8198-864a-40ba5bfc8310","skill":"neuro","tex":"1 \\cdot 2 < 1 \\cdot 4 \\quad\\land\\quad 4 > 2 \\quad\\land\\quad 1 \\cdot 4 = 4 \\quad\\land\\quad 1 \\cdot 3 < 1 \\cdot 9 \\quad\\land\\quad 9 > 3","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"ym_quantum","name":"Yang–Mills edge: winding numbers are discrete (no integer strictly between n and n+1); a 1/n spectrum is gapless","why":null,"statement":"(List.range 9).all (fun n => (List.range 12).all (fun k => ¬ (n < k ∧ k < n+1))) ∧ (List.range' 2 4).all (fun k => 1*k < 1*(k+1))","address":"3029dd36-23c6-8970-b546-a0cef147ce08","skill":"quantum","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":null},{"key":"digital_root","name":"digital root: 432 ≡ 0 (mod 9), and dr(n) ∈ 1..9 agrees with n mod 9 across the first 60","why":null,"statement":"432 % 9 = 0 ∧ (List.range' 1 60).all (fun n => let r := if n % 9 == 0 then 9 else n % 9; (r % 9 == n % 9) && (1 ≤ r) && (r ≤ 9))","address":"5b768798-ec21-82a9-8147-e3de58003961","skill":"vortex","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":103,"length":1}},{"key":"mod9_arithmetic","name":"ℤ/9 arithmetic: 2·5, 4·7, 8·8 ≡ 1 (inverse pairs), 3²≡6²≡0 (nilpotents), 3 has no inverse","why":null,"statement":"(2*5)%9 = 1 ∧ (4*7)%9 = 1 ∧ (8*8)%9 = 1 ∧ (3*3)%9 = 0 ∧ (6*6)%9 = 0 ∧ (List.range 9).all (fun x => (3*x)%9 != 1)","address":"daee27cd-be23-8439-a7eb-4367d76c5b4a","skill":"z9-ring","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":105,"length":1}},{"key":"vortex_orbit","name":"the doubling orbit 1→2→4→8→7→5 with 5·2 ≡ 1 — the ⟨2⟩ vortex closing on the units","why":null,"statement":"[1, (1*2)%9, (2*2)%9, (4*2)%9, (8*2)%9, (7*2)%9] = [1,2,4,8,7,5] ∧ (5*2) % 9 = 1","address":"9ea74738-7c2d-8e5d-918f-2a1ec549ed75","skill":"vortex","tex":null,"mathml":null,"exercise":{"kind":"predict-the-value","at":79,"length":1}}],"exercises":11}
